solution.p:
The expression (20-4^2)(4-6)^3 has two sets of parentheses, so our first step will be to simplify whats inside each of those first according to the order of operations. Once weve done that, well apply the exponent and then finally divide:
\begin{aligned}
(20-4^2)\div(4-6)^3 \amp= (20-\nextoperation{4^2})(4-6)^3\\
\amp= (\nextoperation{20-\highlight{16}})(4-6)^3\\
\amp= \highlight{4}(\nextoperation{4-6})^3\\
\amp= 4\nextoperation{(\highlight{-2})^3}\\
\amp= \nextoperation{4(\highlight{-8})}\\
\amp= \highlight{-32}
\end{aligned}

